    "result": "I implemented `shipping_cost` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and kept the given signature. Inputs are converted to `Decimal` (floats via `str()`, `bool` and other types rejected with `TypeError`). Non-finite numbers are rejected with `ValueError`, which the spec doesn't mention. Dimensions and weight must be positive, subtotal non-negative, and zone must be the plain `int` 1, 2 or 3. Volumetric weight is computed as L×W×H/5000, and the billable weight is the larger of actual and volumetric, rounded up to a 0.5 kg step using `math.ceil` on half-kilogram units. The base charge is 8.00 plus 1.50 per step beyond the first kilogram, multiplied by the zone factor (1, 1.25, 1.6). Free shipping zeroes the base for zones 1 and 2 when the subtotal is at least 150. The 12.00 oversize surcharge is added when the longest side exceeds 120 cm, after the zone factor and free-shipping logic. The total is quantized to two places with `ROUND_HALF_UP` only at the end. Per your instructions, I did not write tests or run anything, so this is verified by reading the code only.",
